  "contract": "Several waits open at once (Workflow DefaultWorkflowTaskBridge applyOpenSignalWait/applyOpenConditionWait, SignalWaits, PendingMessageTask, recordAppliedSignalForSignalResume, recordSatisfiedConditionWaitForSignalResume), over raw worker HTTP on protocol 1.20 in its own namespace. One completion may open any number of signal and condition waits, each with its own sequence, wait id and timeout timer. An accepted signal reserves the latest open wait of its name, unless an earlier signal of that name is still pending, in which case it is buffered. The resumed task applies the signal at its own wait's sequence and cancels that wait's timeout, and also satisfies the latest open condition wait and cancels its timer. A buffered signal whose identity names no open wait is not delivered unless the workflow declares its name; a declared one is delivered and applied at the latest open wait of its name (recordAppliedSignalForSignalResume, openWaitIdForName), and a wait opened later for that name takes the buffered identity (pendingSignalWaitIdForOpenSignalWait). The run summary names the latest open wait; the observation lists every durable wait. Embedded applications have no worker protocol.",
